 	"#str_231306"	"Field of View"
 	"#str_231307"	"Button Prompts"
 	"#str_231308"	"Automatic;Xbox;PlayStation;Nintendo;Steam Deck;Generic"
+	"#str_231309"	"Highlight an option to see what it does."
+	"#str_231310"	"Yes: the mouse looks up and down. No: moving the mouse forward and back walks instead, unless you hold Mouse Look."
+	"#str_231311"	"Reload automatically when the magazine runs empty."
+	"#str_231312"	"Switch to a new weapon automatically when you pick it up."
+	"#str_231313"	"Yes: press zoom once to zoom in and again to zoom out. No: hold zoom to stay zoomed in."
+	"#str_231314"	"Look speed while zoomed or scoped, as a percent of normal. With 360 Controller Feel the stick uses 360 Zoomed Speed instead."
+	"#str_231315"	"How much of the world you see, measured at 4:3; wide screens add more at the sides. Higher sees more, lower looks closer."
+	"#str_231316"	"Show bullet holes, scorch marks and blood on walls and floors."
+	"#str_231317"	"Show your weapon on screen. No hides it for a clearer view."
+	"#str_231318"	"Where your weapon sits on screen: to the right, centered, or lower right."
+	"#str_231319"	"Multiplayer: how pickups look. The original models, simple icons, or flat colored icons with or without a light sweep."
+	"#str_231320"	"Multiplayer: draw the weapons other players hold in flat icon colors, so you can tell what they carry at a glance."
+	"#str_231321"	"Multiplayer: show every player with the bright pro skins, so opponents are easier to spot."
+	"#str_231322"	"Flip vertical mouse look: moving the mouse forward looks down."
+	"#str_231323"	"Blend this many mouse readings together. Higher is smoother but adds a little delay; 1 is off."
+	"#str_231324"	"How fast the view turns when you move the mouse."
+	"#str_231325"	"Your mouse's counts per inch (CPI/DPI), so sensitivity follows real hand movement. 0 keeps the classic sensitivity."
+	"#str_231326"	"Smooth the view by averaging this many recent view angles after the mouse moves. 0 is off."
+	"#str_231327"	"Mouse acceleration, Quake Live style: faster swipes turn farther. Negative values slow fast swipes instead. 0 is off."
+	"#str_231328"	"How fast the mouse must move before acceleration starts."
+	"#str_231329"	"Shape of the acceleration curve. 2 matches Quake Live; higher ramps up more sharply."
+	"#str_231330"	"Upper limit for accelerated sensitivity. 0 means no limit."
+	"#str_231331"	"Use a gamepad. No ignores all controllers."
+	"#str_231332"	"The Xbox 360 version's stick feel (dead zones, look curve, smoothing, turn speeds). Overrides Stick Dead Zone, Look Sensitivity and Look Curve."
+	"#str_231333"	"The Xbox 360 aim assist: stick turning slows while your crosshair is over an enemy, so it is easier to stay on target."
+	"#str_231334"	"Turn speed while your aim is on an enemy, as a percent of normal. Lower feels stickier; 100 turns the slowdown off."
+	"#str_231335"	"360 Controller Feel: left and right turn speed. 0.0253 is the Xbox 360 default."
+	"#str_231336"	"360 Controller Feel: up and down look speed. 0.0209 is the Xbox 360 default."
+	"#str_231337"	"360 Controller Feel: turn speed while zoomed, as a percent of normal. 30 is the Xbox 360 default."
+	"#str_231338"	"Southpaw swaps the sticks: move with the right stick and look with the left."
+	"#str_231339"	"Which button icons to show. Automatic matches the controller you are using."
+	"#str_231340"	"How far a stick must move before it counts. Raise it if the view drifts on its own."
+	"#str_231341"	"How fast the view turns with the look stick."
+	"#str_231342"	"How fast the stick moves the weapon wheel's selection."
+	"#str_231343"	"Moves the weapon wheel left or right. 0 centers it; 27 is the original position."
+	"#str_231344"	"Shapes the look stick's response. Higher makes small movements slower for fine aim, with full speed at the edge."
+	"#str_231345"	"Flip vertical stick look: pushing up looks down."
+	"#str_231346"	"How far a trigger must be pulled before it counts as pressed."
+	"#str_231347"	"Controller vibration when you fire, take damage and more."
+	"#str_231348"	"Vibration strength. 1 is normal; up to 2 is stronger."
+	"#str_231349"	"Aim by tilting a controller that has motion sensors, such as PlayStation and Switch Pro controllers."
+	"#str_231350"	"How far the view turns when you tilt the controller."
+	"#str_231351"	"What the controller's touchpad does: nothing, move the menu cursor, look around, or work only as a button."
+	"#str_231352"	"How fast touchpad movement moves the cursor or the view."
+	"#str_231353"	"Use a touchscreen like a mouse in menus and loading screens."
+	"#str_231354"	"Below this battery percent, vibration is turned down to save power. 0 turns this off."
+	"#str_231355"	"The strongest vibration allowed while the battery is below the Low Battery Rumble level."
+	"#str_231356"	"Weapon Default gives each weapon its own crosshair. Custom uses the crosshair you pick below for every weapon."
+	"#str_231357"	"Pick the custom crosshair."
+	"#str_231358"	"Size of the custom crosshair."
+	"#str_231359"	"Color of the custom crosshair."
+	"#str_231360"	"Flash a marker on the crosshair when your shots hit."
+	"#str_231361"	"HUD style: Classic (the original), Remastered (kept inside the safe area), Minimal (the essentials), or Competitive (multiplayer)."
+	"#str_231362"	"Size of the HUD, separate from the menus."
+	"#str_231363"	"How far the HUD spreads on wide screens: within 16:9, within 21:9, or the full width."
+	"#str_231364"	"Moves the HUD in from the screen edges, in percent of the screen, for TVs that crop the picture."
+	"#str_231365"	"Yes: the objectives button opens and closes your objectives. No: they show only while you hold it."
+	"#str_231366"	"How solid the Remastered HUD is. Lower lets more of the game show through."
+	"#str_231367"	"Show which direction damage is coming from."
+	"#str_231368"	"Show a message when you pick something up."
+	"#str_231369"	"Briefly show your weapon list when you switch weapons."
+	"#str_231370"	"Tone down flashes: limits hit indicators, dims full-screen white flashes and removes the death afterimage."
+	"#str_231371"	"Bodies sink into the floor before they disappear. Ragdoll keeps ragdoll physics while they sink; No Ragdoll turns it off."
+	"#str_231372"	"How long bodies stay before they disappear. Stock keeps the game's own timing."
+	"#str_231373"	"The language for text and speech."
+	"#str_231374"	"The keys that open the console: Tilde alone, or Ctrl+Alt+Tilde so it can't open by accident."
+	"#str_231375"	"Skip cutscenes automatically as soon as they start."
+	"#str_231376"	"Field of view for your weapon only. 0 follows the main Field of View."
+	"#str_231377"	"With a Weapon FOV set: Classic keeps the weapon looking the same on any screen shape; Direct uses the value as is."
+	"#str_231378"	"Moves your weapon left or right on screen."
+	"#str_231379"	"Moves your weapon forward or back."
+	"#str_231380"	"Moves your weapon up or down."
+	"#str_231381"	"Your weapon kicks back on screen when it fires. No holds it still."
+	"#str_231382"	"Play in virtual reality with a connected headset."
+	"#str_231383"	"Aim where your weapon-hand controller points, or where you look."
+	"#str_231384"	"Which hand holds the weapon. Left also moves you with the right stick."
+	"#str_231385"	"Turn in fixed steps (Snap) or smoothly with the stick."
+	"#str_231386"	"How many degrees each snap turn rotates you."
+	"#str_231387"	"Which way the stick walks you: where your head faces, or where your off-hand controller points."
+	"#str_231388"	"Your character follows you as you walk around your room. Disabled keeps it in place."
+	"#str_231389"	"Show where your shots land while aiming with the controller: a dot, or a dot and a laser beam."
+	"#str_231390"	"Controller vibration strength in VR."
+	"#str_231391"	"Grip the front of the gun with your off hand to hold it in both hands."
+	"#str_231392"	"Darkens the edges of your view while you move or turn smoothly, to reduce motion sickness."
+	"#str_231393"	"Crouch in your room to crouch in the game."
 }
